From 84d45a97c3c8a571424520dc6e7a5856595d65b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:13:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] New pages: home strips in place of map links, feeds on the
 buyer pages, FAQ dropdowns, one owner for the builder ranking

Owner, 2026-11-08: "rather than having links to go to the IDX just have the horizontal IDX feed in the blog in
that location", "the buyer pages dont have a highly personalized IDX feed they definitely should", "all the
FAQ's should become dropdown boxes".

- idx-lib: a homes strip may be a feature search (has, from the CRM's list), a town and a price ceiling;
  such strips (listOnly) are never read as a place in a buyer's sentence, and their See-all pages carry
  their own title. Eight strips: pool homes east of US 17 and at $400,000 or less, beach-walk houses in
  North Myrtle Beach (and at $400,000 or less), new homes at $300,000 or less, Market Common townhomes,
  houses listed cash only, houses that list a new roof. Feeds: pool homes, beach-walk houses and new
  homes at the top of their pages; just-listed homes lower on sell-or-buy-first and best-time-to-sell.
- The ten pages: each map link where the article talks about the homes is now a strip.
- mkpage: the FAQ is a list of dropdowns, the first open; each question stays an h3, each answer in the HTML.
- New construction keeps one sentence on the builders and links the builders page, which owns the ranking.
- Seller disclosure: an offer for owners selling alone (coaching, which includes reading the form);
  the FSBO and undisclosed-flooding pages link to the disclosure guide.
- Market Common map: Belle Harbor's name moved inside the phone map.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
