t-align:center;gap:.2rem;padding:.4rem .1rem}.c3-glance .i{width:1.6rem;height:1.6rem}.c3-glance strong{font-size:.875rem}.c3-glance span.t{font-size:1rem;line-height:1.2}}</style><ul role="list" class="c3-glance" style="--n:3"><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><span><strong>5,277 new homes</strong><span class="t">sold to their first owners in Horry County in a year</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5.5 7h8A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 15 8.5v11a1.5 1.5 0 0 1-1.5 1.5h-8A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-11A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 5.5 7zM8 7V4.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 9.5 3h9A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 20 4.5v11a1.5 1.5 0 0 1-1.5 1.5H15M9.5 17.5l-2.3-2.4a1.4 1.4 0 0 1 2.3-1.6 1.4 1.4 0 0 1 2.3 1.6z"/></svg></span><span><strong>15 builders</strong><span class="t">sold 50 or more each</span></span></li><li><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><span><strong>About $335,000</strong><span class="t">middle price of a new home</span></span></li></ul></div><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated November 8, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Every builder that sold 50 or more new homes in a year, the towns it builds in, what its homes are like and what they cost.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">D.R. Horton and Lennar build the most new homes around Myrtle Beach. Together they sold about 45 percent of the 5,277 new homes sold to their first owners in Horry County in a year.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Ryan Homes, Pulte Homes and Meritage Homes come next, and 15 builders sold 50 or more. About 3 in 4 of the new homes are inland, with Conway, Longs and Myrtle Beach addresses.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><p style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">About 1,090 new homes are for sale now. We send you the ones that fit.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Send us your town and price</a></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory);padding-top:2.5rem"><div class="wrap"><nav aria-label="On this page" style="margin-top:0;max-width:720px"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.3rem;font-weight:600">On this page</p><ul style="list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0"><li><a href="#ranking" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Who builds the most</a></li><li><a href="#where" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Where they build</a></li><li><a href="#largest" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">The five largest</a></li><li><a href="#owners" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Other builders</a></li><li><a href="#prices" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">What they cost</a></li><li><a href="#ask" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">Before you sign</a></li><li><a href="#new-home-builders-faq" style="display:block;padding:.65rem 0;color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:.18em;line-height:1.35">New home builders FAQ</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="ranking"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Who builds the most">Which builders build the most new homes around Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">D.R. Horton sold the most, about 1 in 4 of the new homes. Each bar is one builder, with the middle price its buyers paid:</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="New homes each builder sold to a first owner in Horry County"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">New homes each builder sold to a first owner in Horry County</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Builder, middle price</span><span role="columnheader">homes sold</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">D.R. Horton</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $325,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">1,397</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Lennar</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $258,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.692" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">967</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Ryan Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $350,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.341" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">477</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Pulte Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $488,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.273" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">382</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Meritage Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $340,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.224" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">313</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Mungo Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $396,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.147" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">206</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Great Southern Homes, now Stanley Martin</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $326,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.13" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">182</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Beverly Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $324,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.13" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">182</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Beazer Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $393,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.112" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">156</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Dream Finders Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $309,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.107" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">149</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Starlight Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $259,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.106" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">148</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Toll Brothers</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $612,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.072" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">100</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Ashton Woods</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $380,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.067" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">94</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">DRB Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $327,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.044" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">61</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Howell Homes</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">about $318,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.037" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">52</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Our count of county deeds recorded November 2025 to October 2026: houses, townhouses and condos a builder sold to its first owner. Builders that sold 50 or more. The middle price is the one half sold above and half below. We count homes sold and do not rate build quality.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The five largest sold about two-thirds of the new homes. A builder's new home sold for about $335,000 in the middle, against about $306,000 for a home resold by its owner.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Five more sellers are companies that each sell new homes in one community, such as Waterbridge SC LLC in Waterbridge. Their deeds name no builder, so we count them apart. Together they sold 239 homes, mostly with Myrtle Beach and Little River addresses.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">This page counts builders that sell new homes in their own communities. To build on a lot you own, you hire a builder under a construction contract. The license check in the last section applies to that builder too, and our guide gives <a href="/buyers/new-construction/#how-long" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">how long each kind of build takes</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="where"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Where they build">Where does each builder build in Horry County?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Mostly inland, around Conway, Longs and Myrtle Beach. A mailing address is not the city limits: a Myrtle Beach address includes Carolina Forest and Socastee:</p><figure class="bd-map"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 440 430" role="img" aria-label="Map of Horry County with a dot for each place builders sold new homes in 12 months; a larger dot stands for more homes. The largest dots are around Conway, Longs, Myrtle Beach and North Myrtle Beach, and the dots thin out near Loris and Aynor. D.R. Horton's are largest around Conway, Lennar's and Meritage's around Longs, and Pulte's near Myrtle Beach and North Myrtle Beach. Almost none are on the beach itself."><defs><clipPath id="bd-frame"><rect width="440" height="430"/></clipPath><clipPath id="bd-county"><path d="M288.7,337.3L273.1,348.3L264.4,356.2L241.2,379.7L208.9,414.7L162.0,424.1L160.0,426.1L159.5,424.3L126.7,424.8L120.3,423.9L120.2,417.5L121.3,411.2L120.4,402.9L118.3,403.1L117.5,407.8L115.7,408.5L111.6,404.1L109.8,402.4L110.2,399.0L109.6,395.2L107.4,394.3L106.7,391.4L107.1,389.9L104.9,388.4L107.3,386.3L104.5,382.2L105.7,381.4L108.