.55}main#main .c3-place-cta .c3-offer{margin:0;flex:0 1 auto}main#main .detail-hero .detail-sub{display:none}</style><style>.c3-nh-guide{margin:.1rem 0 0}.c3-nh-guide p{margin:0 0 .35rem!important;line-height:1.45}.c3-nh-guide a{white-space:nowrap}.c3-nh-n::before{content:attr(data-n);display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-width:1.45em;height:1.45em;margin:0 .3em 0 .05em;border-radius:999px;font-size:.78em;font-weight:700;line-height:1;color:var(--navy);background:rgba(255,255,255,.85);border:1.5px solid var(--brass-ink,#8a5a2b);vertical-align:.12em}</style><div class="c3-guide c3-guide-map"><style>main#main .c3-gcards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(15rem,1fr));gap:.7rem;max-width:760px;margin:.2rem 0 1rem}main#main .c3-gcard{padding:.75rem .9rem .8rem;border-radius:16px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.55);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.75);box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(28,32,40,.08);backdrop-filter:blur(14px) saturate(140%);-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(14px) saturate(140%)}main#main .c3-gcard h3{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.45rem;margin:0 0 .35rem!important;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.92rem!important;font-weight:650;color:var(--navy);line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gcard h3 .i{display:inline-flex;color:var(--brass)}main#main .c3-gcard .c3-gul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}main#main .c3-gcard .c3-gi{font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.6;margin:0}main#main .c3-gcard a{color:var(--navy)}@media (prefers-reduced-transparency:reduce){main#main .c3-gcard{backdrop-filter:none;-webkit-backdrop-filter:none;background:#fbf8f3}}</style><div class="c3-gcards"><div class="c3-gcard"><h3><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3v13M12 3l7 11h-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span>A boat at home, or a ramp within 10 minutes</h3><ul class="c3-gul"><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#cherry-grove" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline"><span class="c3-nh-n" data-n="7" aria-hidden="true"></span>Cherry Grove</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#little-river" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline"><span class="c3-nh-n" data-n="8" aria-hidden="true"></span>Little River</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#socastee" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline"><span class="c3-nh-n" data-n="9" aria-hidden="true"></span>Socastee</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#surfside-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline"><span class="c3-nh-n" data-n="10" aria-hidden="true"></span>Surfside Beach</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#murrells-inlet" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline"><span class="c3-nh-n" data-n="12" aria-hidden="true"></span>Murrells Inlet</a></li></ul></div><div class="c3-gcard"><h3><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11a9 7.5 0 0 1 18 0q-2.25-1.5-4.5 0t-4.5 0-4.5 0-4.5 0zM12 11v8M2.5 21.5c3-1.4 6.3-1.4 9.5 0s6.5 1.4 9.5 0"/></svg></span>Most houses within half a mile of the sand</h3><ul class="c3-gul"><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#downtown-myrtle-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline"><span class="c3-nh-n" data-n="1" aria-hidden="true"></span>Downtown Myrtle Beach</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#myrtle-heights" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline"><span class="c3-nh-n" data-n="2" aria-hidden="true"></span>Myrtle Heights</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#windy-hill" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline"><span class="c3-nh-n" data-n="4" aria-hidden="true"></span>Windy Hill</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#crescent-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline"><span class="c3-nh-n" data-n="5" aria-hidden="true"></span>Crescent Beach</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#ocean-drive" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline"><span class="c3-nh-n" data-n="6" aria-hidden="true"></span>Ocean Drive</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#garden-city-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline"><span class="c3-nh-n" data-n="11" aria-hidden="true"></span>Garden City</a></li></ul></div><div class="c3-gcard"><h3><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 16v-4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h10.5l2 5M14.5 11l4-7H21M8.5 17.5h4M2 21.5h20"/><circle cx="6.5" cy="17.5" r="2"/><circle cx="14.5" cy="17.5" r="2"/></svg></span>Room to spread out</h3><ul class="c3-gul"><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#pine-lakes" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline"><span class="c3-nh-n" data-n="3" aria-hidden="true"></span>Pine Lakes' older streets</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#country-around-loris" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline"><span class="c3-nh-n" data-n="15" aria-hidden="true"></span>Around Loris</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#aynor" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline"><span class="c3-nh-n" data-n="16" aria-hidden="true"></span>Aynor</a></li></ul></div><div class="c3-gcard"><h3><span class="i"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 21h18M5 21V9.5l5-3V21M10 21V4h9v17M13 8h3M13 12h3M13 16h3M7.5 13h.01M7.5 16.5h.01"/></svg></span>A small town with old streets</h3><ul class="c3-gul"><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#conway" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline"><span class="c3-nh-n" data-n="13" aria-hidden="true"></span>Conway</a></li><li class="c3-gi"><a href="#loris" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline"><span class="c3-nh-n" data-n="14" aria-hidden="true"></span>Loris</a></li></ul></div></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="downtown-myrtle-beach"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="1. Downtown">1. Downtown Myrtle Beach: the boardwalk on foot</h2><div class="c3-nh-chips"><span class="c3-nh-chip">Listed with no HOA fee: nearly 9 in 10 homes for sale</span></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From the older streets downtown, you can walk to the oceanfront <a href="https://www.myrtlebeachboardwalk.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">boardwalk</a>. From Collins Street it is about a quarter hour on foot. From the day after Labor Day through April, you can ride a bike or walk a dog on it at any hour.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nohoa-downtown-myrtle-beach" data-name="Downtown Myrtle Beach"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/downtown-myrtle-beach-pleasant-inn-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/downtown-myrtle-beach-pleasant-inn-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/downtown-myrtle-beach-pleasant-inn-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A two-story white wood house with long porches on both floors, shaded by big oak trees with Spanish moss, on Broadway Street in downtown Myrtle Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pubdog. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Pubdog</a></span></div><figcaption>The Pleasant Inn, a wood guest house from about 1927, under the live oaks on Broadway Street, in the old town by Withers Swash.</figcaption></figure></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most of these houses are within half a mile of the beach. All of them are outside the high-risk flood zones, where the federal rule makes a lender require flood insurance.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Plyler Park on the oceanfront has free live music and a <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R2620.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">fireworks show</a> on Wednesdays in summer. The older houses are on Collins, Chester and Dunbar Streets, and Spivey Park and the New Town Bark Park are on Collins Street too.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A trail with a wooden boardwalk is beside Withers Swash, one of the city's <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/i_want_to/find/photos_of_the_week/pow040618.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">oldest waterways</a>, from Third Avenue South to Broadway and Collins Street.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Lots are modest, about 9,000 square feet in a typical case. Inside the city, a camper may not be kept in the front yard, so it has to fit beside or behind the house.</p><p class="c3-place-price">Houses with no HOA fee here are listed at about $435,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="myrtle-heights"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="2. Myrtle Heights">2. Myrtle Heights: a beach path at the end of each avenue</h2><div class="c3-nh-chips"><span class="c3-nh-chip">Listed with no HOA fee: every home for sale</span></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In Myrtle Heights, the plan of the mid-1930s carried the avenues through to the beach, and those ends now give public access to the sand. From every house for sale here, a beach access is less than 5 minutes away on foot.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nohoa-myrtle-heights" data-name="Myrtle Heights"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/myrtle-heights-older-house-on-ocean-boulevard-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/myrtle-heights-older-house-on-ocean-boulevard-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/myrtle-heights-older-house-on-ocean-boulevard-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="An older two-story white wood house with tall columns, black shutters and a brick chimney, on a grassy rise above North Ocean Boulevard in Myrtle Heights" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pubdog. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Pubdog</a></span></div><figcaption>An older two-story house with columns on North Ocean Boulevard, in the Myrtle Heights-Oak Park Historic District.</figcaption></figure></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The same plan set a minimum setback of 75 feet for oceanfront houses. The district is on the <a href="https://npgallery.nps.gov/AssetDetail/NRIS/96001217" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">National Register of Historic Places</a>, which calls the Myrtle Heights-Oak Park district the largest intact group of historic properties in Myrtle Beach.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The houses, built from about 1925 to 1945, are mostly two-story frame homes, many with a garage or a garage apartment. You will see porches and wood awnings painted solid or striped to look like canvas. A few houses keep old walls of coquina rock or brick.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Back yards along Ocean Boulevard often have native wax myrtles, the plant the city is named for, along with red cedars, palmettos and windswept oaks.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Sea Captain's House, a restaurant in a 1930 beach cottage, is about a 9-minute walk from the middle of Myrtle Heights.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On an oceanfront house, a change to the outside, including its color, needs the city's <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/government/boards_and_committees/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Community Appearance Board</a>. Ordinary repair does not.</p><p class="c3-place-price">Houses with no HOA fee here are listed at about $1.6 million.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="pine-lakes"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="3. Pine Lakes">3. Pine Lakes' older streets: almost half an acre in the middle of the city</h2><div class="c3-nh-chips"><span class="c3-nh-chip">Listed with no HOA fee: every home for sale on the older streets</span></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The older Pine Lakes streets have big lots in the middle of the city: typically almost half an acre, more than twice a downtown lot. There is room for a workshop or a boat beside the house.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nohoa-pine-lakes" data-name="Pine Lakes' older streets"></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The streets are around the golf course, which is <a href="https://www.pinelakes.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">less than half a mile from the ocean</a>, on rolling land. The beach is about 0.6 mile on foot, at the Seaside Place street end, one of the city's fully accessible beach paths.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.myrtlebeachprst.com/_T4_R41.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ocean Forest Memorial Park</a>, with a walking path, is at the Haskell Circle beach access, about half a mile on foot. North Ocean Boulevard has bike lanes.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A resident whose car is registered and taxed in the city gets a free parking decal. With it, you park free at city meters, at beach street ends and at <a href="https://www.milb.com/myrtle-beach/ballpark/pelicans-ballpark-a-z" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pelicans baseball games</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The city picks up trash, recycling and yard waste at the curb each week, for about $34 a month.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Preserve at Pine Lakes, the newer section, has an HOA fee and is not counted here.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You pay for the room: houses here are listed at more than twice the downtown price, for more than twice the land.</p><p class="c3-place-price">Houses with no HOA fee here are listed at about $930,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="windy-hill"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="4. Windy Hill">4. Windy Hill: free day docks at Barefoot Landing</h2><div class="c3-nh-chips"><span class="c3-nh-chip">Listed with no HOA fee: 6 in 10 homes for sale</span></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Windy Hill is 3 minutes by car from Barefoot Landing on the Intracoastal Waterway. Come by boat, and you can <a href="https://www.bflanding.com/plan-your-visit/day-docking/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">use the finger docks</a> free for the day while you shop or eat.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nohoa-windy-hill" data-name="Windy Hill"></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Alabama Theatre and House of Blues are on the same grounds. Barefoot Landing welcomes leashed pets all year, and many of its shops let them inside.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most houses for sale here are within a 10-minute walk of a public beach access. Inside North Myrtle Beach, a work truck up to 18,500 pounds may park at home.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On 41st Avenue South, a <a href="https://www.nmb.us/474/41st-Avenue-South-Pocket-Park" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">pocket park</a> with garden plantings, two pergolas and a walking path is on the site of the old water tower. Conway investors developed Windy Hill after World War II, and in 1968 it joined Cherry Grove, Ocean Drive and Crescent Beach to form North Myrtle Beach.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Flood is the cost here. About half of these houses are in a high-risk flood zone, and with a mortgage your lender will almost always require flood insurance.</p><p class="c3-place-price">Houses with no HOA fee here are listed at about $745,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="crescent-beach"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="5. Crescent Beach">5. Crescent Beach: half a mile on foot to a beach access</h2><div class="c3-nh-chips"><span class="c3-nh-chip">Listed with no HOA fee: nearly 9 in 10 homes for sale</span></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most houses for sale in Crescent Beach are less than half a mile on foot from a public beach access. From 6th to 27th Avenue South, the beach is one of the city's three <a href="https://www.nmb.us/219/Surfing-Rules-Regulations" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">surf zones</a>. From mid-May to mid-September, boards are banned from 9 to 4 on the rest of the beach, but you can surf here.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nohoa-crescent-beach" data-name="Crescent Beach"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/crescent-beach-streets-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/crescent-beach-streets-from-the-ocean-2011-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/crescent-beach-streets-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="782" alt="Streets of two-story beach houses among trees behind the oceanfront at Crescent Beach in North Myrtle Beach, seen from a plane over the ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Crescent Beach from over the ocean in 2011: streets of beach houses behind the oceanfront.</figcaption></figure></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://nmb.us/783/Ingram-Dunes-Nature-Preserve" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ingram Dunes Nature Preserve</a>, on Hillside Drive, is the city's last remaining maritime forest. It has native dunes 30 feet tall and an interpretive half-mile nature trail.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most are older beach houses, on streets such as Hillside Drive, Holly Drive, Perrin Drive and Strand Avenue. Few of them need flood insurance for a mortgage. In Cherry Grove, almost every home does.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the middle of Crescent Beach, the <a href="https://www.nmb.us/782/18th-Edge-Pocket-Park" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">18th and Edge pocket park</a> has benches and a fountain. <a href="https://www.nmb.us/475/Central-Park" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Central Park</a>, 20 acres with lighted tennis courts, pickleball courts and a paved walking path, is about 0.7 mile away.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">City beach lots charge for parking from March through October. <a href="https://www.nmb.us/545/Parking-Registration-Information" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Residents register their plates</a> each year for free passes.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Lots are small, about 7,600 square feet. Under the city's rule, a trailer or camper goes behind the front of the house or under a carport. That takes a carport, or room beside or behind the house.</p><p class="c3-place-price">Houses with no HOA fee here are listed at about $755,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="ocean-drive"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="6. Ocean Drive">6. Ocean Drive: Main Street and the shag</h2><div class="c3-nh-chips"><span class="c3-nh-chip">Listed with no HOA fee: more than half the homes for sale</span></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On Main Street in Ocean Drive, you can learn the shag free on Tuesday nights. <a href="https://www.fatharolds.com" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Fat Harold's Beach Club</a> calls itself the Home of the Shag and teaches the dance.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nohoa-ocean-drive" data-name="Ocean Drive"></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the Ocean Drive and Crescent Beach area, a pavilion and amusement park drew crowds who danced the shag.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A Saturday here can start with breakfast at <a href="https://www.hoskinsrestaurant.com" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hoskins Restaurant</a> on Main Street, which opened in 1948.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The <a href="https://www.northmyrtlebeachmuseum.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">North Myrtle Beach Area Historical Museum</a> is free, and its exhibits include beach music artists and shag dancing. <a href="https://www.nmb.us/493/McLean-Park" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">McLean Park</a>, a quarter mile from Hoskins on foot, has a two-acre lake and a half-mile paved walking path.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each summer, the city holds free Music on Main concerts on Thursdays at the Horseshoe. Each December, a nighttime Christmas parade comes up Main Street. Few of the houses for sale here with no fee need flood insurance for a mortgage.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Crowds come with it: on concert nights Main Street closes to cars in the afternoon, and the St. Patrick's festival draws about 40,000 people.</p><p class="c3-place-price">Houses with no HOA fee here are listed at about $665,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="cherry-grove"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="7. Cherry Grove">7. Cherry Grove: a boat on the canals</h2><div class="c3-nh-chips"><span class="c3-nh-chip">Listed with no HOA fee: more than half the homes for sale</span></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Cherry Grove's canals were created as early as the 1950s. The city <a href="https://www.myhorrynews.com/news/local/north_myrtle_beach/residents-still-paying-for-cherry-grove-dredge/article_1eb5bb32-3b9a-11e9-93e7-9f8ad503b643.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">has dredged canals there twice since 2016</a>, to give owners boat access to House Creek and the Intracoastal Waterway at high and low tide.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nohoa-cherry-grove" data-name="Cherry Grove"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/cherry-grove-canals-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/cherry-grove-canals-from-the-ocean-2011-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/cherry-grove-canals-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="782" alt="Rows of houses on long canals with boat docks, running back from the beach to a wide green marsh at Cherry Grove, seen from a plane over the ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Cherry Grove from over the ocean in 2011: houses on the canals, many with their own docks, and the marsh behind.</figcaption></figure></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The city's <a href="https://nmb.us/490/Cherry-Grove-Park-and-Boat-Ramp" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">boat ramp at 53rd Avenue North</a> reaches both the marsh and the open ocean through Hog Inlet. It has a two-lane boat launch, a kayak launch, a fishing pier, a floating boat dock and a fish cleaning station.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Myrtle Beach residents park free at the ramp when they register with the city. It is also the way in to Heritage Shores Nature Preserve, an island in the marsh reached on elevated boardwalks.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Many of the canal houses have their own docks, so the boat stays behind the house. Across Hog Inlet, Waties Island has almost three miles of undeveloped beach.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each July 4, the city's free fireworks go up at the Cherry Grove Pier. The homes here with an HOA fee are all in named subdivisions.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Two costs come with the canals: flood insurance and a dredging fee. Almost every home here is in a high-risk flood zone. Owners of about 415 properties in the canal district pay the city about $1,700 a year for the dredging, on the county tax bill.</p><p class="c3-place-price">Houses with no HOA fee here are listed at about $850,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="little-river"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="8. Little River">8. Little River: the old fishing village on the waterway</h2><div class="c3-nh-chips"><span class="c3-nh-chip">Listed with no HOA fee: every home for sale</span></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The houses on Little River's old waterfront streets are less than a mile from the docks on Mineola Avenue, on the Intracoastal Waterway. Local boatmen began <a href="https://www.saltwaterfishing.sc.gov/pdf/littleriverpart1.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">taking visitors fishing for a fee</a> there, probably in the early 1920s. They ran the first organized offshore fishing trips for visitors in South Carolina.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nohoa-little-river" data-name="Little River"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/little-river-waterway-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/little-river-waterway-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/little-river-waterway-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Little River from above: houses on wooded streets, a marina with boat slips at the lower left, docks running across a salt marsh labelled Salt marsh, and dark water labelled Intracoastal Waterway at the lower right" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>The old Little River waterfront from the air: streets of houses beside the salt marsh and the Intracoastal Waterway.</figcaption></figure></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.hurricanejuels.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hurricane Juel's</a>, with a view of the waterway, has been family owned since 1945.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The waterfront holds the <a href="https://www.bluecrabfestival.org/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Blue Crab Festival</a> each May, on the weekend after Mother's Day; a TV station reported more than 30,000 people there in 2026. <a href="https://littlerivershrimpfest.org/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ShrimpFest</a> follows each October. On the Saturday after Thanksgiving, a <a href="https://www.christmasregatta.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">lighted boat parade</a> leaves Little River Inlet and heads down the waterway.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The county's <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/parksandrecreation/boat-landings/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">T. Craig Campbell boat landing</a> is on the waterway in town. After the inlet's jetties were finished in 1983, boats could cross the bar at any time of day. The state keeps an <a href="https://www.dnr.sc.gov/marine/pub/seascience/reefloc.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">artificial fishing reef</a> off the inlet.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/parksandrecreation/parks/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vereen Memorial Historical Gardens</a>, a county park on the waterway, has about 3 miles of trails and boardwalks through its gardens and along the water. Some of the houses for sale are new, on Mineola and Ellis Avenues; others are on McCorsley Avenue and Bayshore Drive.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The beach takes a drive: none of these houses is within a mile of the ocean.</p><p class="c3-place-price">Houses with no HOA fee here are listed at about $420,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="socastee"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="9. Socastee">9. Socastee: a county boat ramp 2 minutes away</h2><div class="c3-nh-chips"><span class="c3-nh-chip">Listed with no HOA fee: most homes for sale</span></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/parksandrecreation/boat-landings/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Rosewood Landing</a>, a county boat ramp on the Intracoastal Waterway, is 2 minutes by car from these streets. Socastee Landing and Park has a second ramp and a new accessible playground. The swing bridge at Socastee, finished in 1935, marked the completion of the Intracoastal Waterway in South Carolina. The waterway's opening celebration was held in Socastee in April 1936.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nohoa-socastee" data-name="Socastee"></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">These streets are outside any town, so the county's rules apply. County zoning names no limit on where you park a boat. Outdoor storage may not be in front of the house, and a small shed can go 5 feet from the line.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most are 1980s houses in Rosewood Estates and Cimerron Plantation.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/parksandrecreation/parks/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Socastee Recreation Park</a> has fields, picnic areas, disc golf, trails and a playground. Market Common and Coastal Grand Mall are each about 10 minutes away, and the beach at Surfside is about 15 minutes by car.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Flood insurance is the extra cost to plan for: about a third of these houses need it if you buy with a mortgage.</p><p class="c3-place-price">Houses with no HOA fee here are listed at about $250,000, the lowest on this page.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="surfside-beach"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="10. Surfside Beach">10. Surfside Beach: two boats at home and golf carts on the streets</h2><div class="c3-nh-chips"><span class="c3-nh-chip">Listed with no HOA fee: nearly 9 in 10 homes for sale</span></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In Surfside Beach, the town allows up to two boats or trailers at a home, and only one over 21 feet. A permitted golf cart may be driven in daylight within four miles of home, on streets posted at 35 miles an hour or less.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nohoa-surfside-beach" data-name="Surfside Beach"></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town has <a href="https://www.scencyclopedia.org/sce/entries/surfside-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">live oaks well over a century old</a> and <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/200/Beaches" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">36 public beach accesses</a>. In 2016 Surfside Beach became the first town certified autism-friendly through the Champion Autism Network.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town holds a <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/325/Surfside-Beach-Farmers-Market" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">farmers market</a> on Tuesdays from spring into December in Memorial Park, and free Sunday afternoon concerts there from late May through August. Each July 4, a <a href="https://www.surfsidebeach.org/367/4th-of-July-Golf-Cart-Parade" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">golf cart parade</a> goes down Ocean Boulevard.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each October, the fall festival has more than 100 craft vendors. Fireworks may be set off on the sand from sunset on July 4 and on New Year's Eve, but not within 500 feet of the pier.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town picks up trash at the curb, and it has more than nine miles of sidewalk.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">One cost to know on the ocean side: about 1 in 4 homes there needs flood insurance if you buy with a mortgage.</p><p class="c3-place-price">Houses with no HOA fee here are listed at about $940,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="garden-city-beach"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="11. Garden City">11. Garden City Beach: a free pier walk and free beach parking</h2><div class="c3-nh-chips"><span class="c3-nh-chip">Listed with no HOA fee: most homes for sale</span></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.gardencitypier.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Pier at Garden City</a> is always free to walk, and every oceanfront beach access in Garden City has <a href="https://horrycountysc.gov/departments/parksandrecreation/beach-accesses/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">free parking all year</a>. On summer nights, live bands play at both ends of the pier.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nohoa-garden-city-beach" data-name="Garden City Beach"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/garden-city-beach-and-marsh-from-the-ocean-2011-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="782" alt="Beach houses in rows between the ocean beach and a wide marsh with tidal creeks and boat docks at Garden City Beach, seen from a plane over the ocean" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Garden City Beach from over the ocean in 2011: rows of houses between the beach and the marsh, with docks on the creeks behind.</figcaption></figure></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A pier pass covers fishing, so you need no state license. Its Hugo burger is named for the 1989 hurricane that destroyed the pier.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most of the houses for sale here are within half a mile of the shore. The county's Stanley Drive landing is a 5-minute drive.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each July 4, decorated boats start at the point of Garden City Beach and parade through Murrells Inlet.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Budget for flood insurance: with a mortgage, a lender will almost always require it on most of these houses.</p><p class="c3-place-price">Houses with no HOA fee here are listed at about $1.4 million.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="murrells-inlet"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="12. Murrells Inlet">12. Murrells Inlet's north end: by the creeks and the county boat ramp</h2><div class="c3-nh-chips"><span class="c3-nh-chip">Listed with no HOA fee: almost all homes for sale</span></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At the north end of Murrells Inlet, some of the houses for sale are on the creeks of the inlet, and the rest are a few streets back. The county's <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/parksandrecreation/boat-landings/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">boat landing on Stanley Drive</a> is a 4-minute drive, and several houses on the market lately have their own floating dock.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nohoa-murrells-inlet" data-name="Murrells Inlet's north end"></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">People first came to the inlet for oyster roasts and fried shore dinners, and seafood restaurants followed. The <a href="https://www.marshwalk.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MarshWalk</a>, a half-mile wooden boardwalk along the salt marsh with a row of restaurants, is about 6 minutes away by car. The writer Mickey Spillane made Murrells Inlet his home for decades.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The free pier walk and free beach parking at Garden City Beach are a 6-minute drive across the marsh. <a href="https://www.scencyclopedia.org/sce/entries/brookgreen-gardens/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Brookgreen Gardens</a>, with its sculpture gardens on four former rice plantations, is about 15 minutes away by car.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Murrells Inlet is not a town, so the county's rules apply on most of these streets. The south part is in Georgetown County. There, a vehicle or travel trailer without current plates has to be kept in a closed building.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Flood is the honest cost: more than half of these houses are in a high-risk flood zone.</p><p class="c3-place-price">Houses with no HOA fee here are listed at about $820,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="conway"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="13. Conway">13. Conway: live oaks and the Waccamaw River</h2><div class="c3-nh-chips"><span class="c3-nh-chip">Listed with no HOA fee: nearly 9 in 10 homes for sale</span></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Conway's older streets <a href="http://www.conwaysc.gov/news_detail_T6_R144.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">were designed around its live oaks</a>, on a bluff of the Waccamaw River. The Riverwalk follows the river downtown, and the Waccamaw is a federal <a href="https://www.conwaysc.gov/Waccamaw-River-Blue-Trail-Waterproof-Booklet-2020-Digital.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">National Water Trail</a>.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nohoa-conway" data-name="Conway"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A wooden boardwalk with a black railing, shaded by trees, beside old wooden buildings in Conway" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pubdog. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Pubdog</a></span></div><figcaption>The Riverwalk in downtown Conway, on the Waccamaw River.</figcaption></figure></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In town, lots are about 15,000 square feet. Inside the city, a camper or a trailer can go in the side or back yard or under a carport. A shed goes in back, with a permit.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The oldest streets form a <a href="https://schpr.sc.gov/index.php/Detail/objects/S10817726031" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">National Register district</a>. Its houses range from Greek Revival and Carpenter Gothic through Queen Anne to 1920s bungalows, one of them with a porch around three sides. City Hall is the old Horry County courthouse, finished in 1825 to a design credited to Robert Mills. Its courtroom still holds city court every week.</p><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/conway-older-house-and-oak-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/conway-older-house-and-oak-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/conway-older-house-and-oak-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="An older white wood house with black shutters behind a large oak tree, with a paved driveway, a low brick planter and thick shrubs, on a shaded street in Conway" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pubdog. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Pubdog</a></span></div><figcaption>An older house behind a big oak in Conway's residential historic district.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The <a href="https://www.horrycountymuseum.org/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County Museum</a> is in the restored 1905 Burroughs School, about a quarter hour on foot from downtown. <a href="https://www.conwayriverfest.com/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Riverfest</a> brings music and fireworks to the river on the Saturday before the Fourth of July weekend, and the Celebration of Lights opens each December.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/parksandrecreation/boat-landings/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Billy Witherspoon Landing</a>, a county ramp on the Waccamaw, is a 6-minute drive. Conway Medical Center is a 12-minute drive.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The beach is a 25-minute drive.</p><p class="c3-place-price">Houses with no HOA fee here are listed at about $285,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="loris"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="14. Loris">14. Loris: a small town with its own hospital</h2><div class="c3-nh-chips"><span class="c3-nh-chip">Listed with no HOA fee: almost all homes for sale</span></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Loris is a small town with its own hospital: McLeod Loris, with an emergency room, is in town. The older houses were built from the 1940s to the 1970s, on lots of about 0.4 acre. By 1914 Loris was known as the Gate City, because it was the first town on the railroad south of the North Carolina line.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nohoa-loris" data-name="Loris"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/loris-downtown-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/loris-downtown-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/loris-downtown-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="510" alt="Main Street in downtown Loris, South Carolina, with low brick shop buildings, trees and traffic lights" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pithon314. License: CC0" title="License: CC0">Photo: Pithon314</a></span></div><figcaption>Main Street in downtown Loris.</figcaption></figure></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">City zoning allows up to two buildings beside the house, a garage or carport included, so there is room for a workshop. A work truck up to 2 tons may park at home.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Main Street <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/news/articles/rooted-in-community-loris-library-celebrates-50-years-on-main-street/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">library</a> lends cake pans, state park passes and Wi-Fi hotspots.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On the third Saturday in October, the city holds the <a href="https://cityoflorissc.com/about-us" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Loris Bog-Off</a> downtown, with vendors, a car show and live music. The festival's dish is chicken bog: chicken, rice and sausage.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You drive more from here: the beach is about 35 minutes by car.</p><p class="c3-place-price">Houses with no HOA fee here are listed at about $320,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="country-around-loris"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="15. Around Loris">15. The country around Loris: new houses on large lots</h2><div class="c3-nh-chips"><span class="c3-nh-chip">Listed with no HOA fee: most homes for sale</span></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Around Loris, most houses for sale are new, built in 2024 or later, outside any town limits. Many of the new houses are on lots of about 0.7 acre, with room for a camper, a trailer and a shop under the county's rules.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nohoa-country-around-loris" data-name="The country around Loris"></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The <a href="https://sctrails.net/trails/trail/waccamaw-river-heritage-preserve-canoe" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Waccamaw River Heritage Preserve</a> protects 28 miles of the Waccamaw River, with riverside camping on its land.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a work truck, the county lets a business run from home keep three service vehicles on a farm-zoned lot under an acre and a half. McLeod Loris hospital is about 9 minutes away by car.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Outside the towns, a small shed can go 5 feet from the line, and fences can be 8 feet tall. The Solid Waste Authority provides no curbside trash pickup there, so you hire a hauler or use a county drop-off center.</p><p class="c3-place-price">Houses with no HOA fee here are listed at about $415,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="aynor"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="16. Aynor">16. Aynor: an acre and a river landing</h2><div class="c3-nh-chips"><span class="c3-nh-chip">Listed with no HOA fee: most homes for sale</span></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Around Aynor, lots are typically about an acre, with room beside the house for a boat or a camper. More than half of the houses for sale here are new.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="nohoa-aynor" data-name="Aynor"></div><div class="hx-fallback"><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/aynor-country-lot-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/aynor-country-lot-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/aynor-country-lot-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A country road outside Aynor from above, with houses on wide lots among pine trees and fields; one deep lot of about an acre is outlined in orange, with its house labelled near the road" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Houses on lots of about an acre along a country road outside Aynor, from the air. The orange line is one lot.</figcaption></figure></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Galivants Ferry Landing, a county ramp on the <a href="https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/02135000/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Little Pee Dee River</a>, is about 6 minutes from the center of town. The Little Pee Dee is <a href="https://www.townofaynor.gov/appeal" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">popular with canoes, kayaks and small powerboats</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At <a href="https://npgallery.nps.gov/GetAsset/aa6c6bf6-8036-4d76-84bb-d1eb0e3431fd" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Galivants Ferry</a>, the old farm houses have full-width front porches on brick piers. Some were built from wood cut on the farm itself, and the district has log tobacco barns. Galivants Ferry has also held a political speaking, the Stump, since 1880.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each September, <a href="https://www.townofaynor.gov/community" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">almost 25,000 people</a> come to the Aynor Harvest Hoe-Down, a festival the Pilot Club of Aynor started. In the town of Aynor, zoning does not limit a camper or a work truck at home. Most of these houses are outside the town, under county rules.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You will drive more: about 45 minutes to the beach, and about 30 to the nearest hospital, Conway Medical Center.</p><p class="c3-place-price">Houses with no HOA fee here are listed at about $370,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="boats-and-work-trucks"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What you can do at home">What can you do at home with no HOA?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">With no HOA, the limits on parking, rentals and buildings on your lot are the town's, or the county's outside the towns, along with any deed restriction. Most of the homes with no HOA fee around Conway, Loris and Aynor are outside the town limits, under the county's rules.</p><style>.c3-nh-rules{width:100%;max-width:1100px;border-collapse:separate;border-spacing:0 .7rem;margin:1rem 0 1.2rem}.c3-nh-rules caption{text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:.2rem}.c3-nh-rules th,.c3-nh-rules td{vertical-align:top;text-align:left;font-size:1rem;line-height:1.45;padding:.75rem .8rem;background:rgba(255,255,255,.62);border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.95);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.95)}.c3-nh-rules thead th{background:none;border:0;font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);font-size:.95rem;padding:.2rem .8rem}.c3-nh-rules thead th .ic{margin-right:.45rem;vertical-align:middle}.c3-nh-rules tbody th{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.15rem;color:var(--navy);border-left:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.95);border-radius:18px 0 0 18px;white-space:nowrap}.c3-nh-rules tbody td:last-child{border-right:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.95);border-radius:0 18px 18px 0}.c3-nh-rules tbody th small{display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.85rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--muted)}.c3-nh-rules td .ic,.c3-nh-rules td .c3-nh-k{display:none}.c3-nh-rules .ic{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:11px;color:var(--brass);background:rgba(255,255,255,.8);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.95);box-shadow:0 6px 14px -10px rgba(28,32,40,.4)}.c3-nh-sr{position:absolute!important;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}@media (max-width:899px){.c3-nh-rules,.c3-nh-rules tbody,.c3-nh-rules tr,.c3-nh-rules th,.c3-nh-rules td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-nh-rules thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)}.c3-nh-rules caption{display:block;width:auto;margin-bottom:.7rem}.c3-nh-rules tbody tr{margin:0 0 .9rem;border-radius:22px;padding:.9rem 1rem .5rem;background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(255,255,255,.8),rgba(255,255,255,.56));border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.9);box-shadow:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.8),0 18px 40px -28px rgba(28,32,40,.45)}.c3-nh-rules tbody th,.c3-nh-rules tbody td{background:none;border:0!important;border-radius:0!important;padding:0;white-space:normal}.c3-nh-rules tbody th{margin:0 0 .55rem}.c3-nh-rules tbody td{display:grid;grid-template-columns:32px 1fr;gap:.6rem;align-items:start;margin:0 0 .65rem}.c3-nh-rules td .ic{display:inline-flex}.c3-nh-rules td .c3-nh-k{display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.85rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.01em;color:var(--brass-ink,#8a5a2b);margin:0 0 .1rem}}</style><table class="c3-nh-rules"><caption>What you can do at home, by town</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col"><span class="c3-nh-sr">Where the home is</span></th><th scope="col"><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3v13M12 3l7 11h-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span>Boat</th><th scope="col"><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2 6h11v10H2zM13 9h4.5L21 12.5V16h-8"/><circle cx="6" cy="17.5" r="1.8"/><circle cx="17" cy="17.5" r="1.8"/></svg></span>Work truck</th><th scope="col"><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span>Short-term rental</th><th scope="col"><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11l9-6 9 6M5 10v10h14V10M10 20v-5h4v5"/></svg></span>Shed or fence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Outside the towns<small>Horry County</small></th><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3v13M12 3l7 11h-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Boat</span>County zoning names no limit on where you park a boat, but outdoor storage may not be in front of the house.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2 6h11v10H2zM13 9h4.5L21 12.5V16h-8"/><circle cx="6" cy="17.5" r="1.8"/><circle cx="17" cy="17.5" r="1.8"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Work truck</span>A business run from home may keep two service vehicles per acre, and three per home on small farm-zoned lots.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Short-term rental</span>Only in some zones. County zoning does not list short stays, so the zoning office decides where one fits, and short stays pay county taxes.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11l9-6 9 6M5 10v10h14V10M10 20v-5h4v5"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Shed or fence</span>One small shed can sit 5 feet from the line. Fences can be 8 feet tall; over 7 feet needs a permit.</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/submarkets/myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Beach</a></th><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3v13M12 3l7 11h-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Boat</span>A boat over 16 feet, or a camper of any size, stays out of the front yard.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2 6h11v10H2zM13 9h4.5L21 12.5V16h-8"/><circle cx="6" cy="17.5" r="1.8"/><circle cx="17" cy="17.5" r="1.8"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Work truck</span>Yes, one, and no vehicle over one ton.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Short-term rental</span>Only in some zones: the resort and business zones and one residential zone, not the single-family zones.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11l9-6 9 6M5 10v10h14V10M10 20v-5h4v5"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Shed or fence</span>Yes, with a permit. Fences are 4 feet in front and up to 8 in back, but 4 feet all around on an oceanfront lot.</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/submarkets/north-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">North Myrtle Beach</a></th><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3v13M12 3l7 11h-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Boat</span>Yes, behind the front of the house or under a carport.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2 6h11v10H2zM13 9h4.5L21 12.5V16h-8"/><circle cx="6" cy="17.5" r="1.8"/><circle cx="17" cy="17.5" r="1.8"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Work truck</span>Yes, up to 18,500 pounds.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Short-term rental</span>Yes: zoning does not generally limit it. You need a business license, and it does not pass to you when the home sells.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11l9-6 9 6M5 10v10h14V10M10 20v-5h4v5"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Shed or fence</span>One shed up to 150 square feet, behind the house, in most home zones. East of Ocean Boulevard, side-yard fences are not allowed, except low rail fences, pool fences and glass-topped fences.</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/submarkets/surfside-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Surfside Beach</a></th><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3v13M12 3l7 11h-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Boat</span>Yes, up to two boats or trailers, but a licensed trailer over 21 feet counts as one per home. An unlicensed boat goes in a garage or under a cover.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2 6h11v10H2zM13 9h4.5L21 12.5V16h-8"/><circle cx="6" cy="17.5" r="1.8"/><circle cx="17" cy="17.5" r="1.8"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Work truck</span>Yes, one van or pickup up to 21 feet long and 7 feet 11 inches high.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Short-term rental</span>Only in some zones: stays under 30 days are allowed in two zones. Rentals of a year or more are allowed wherever homes are.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11l9-6 9 6M5 10v10h14V10M10 20v-5h4v5"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Shed or fence</span>Yes, in the back yard, with a permit. Fences are 4 feet in front and 6 in back.</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/submarkets/conway/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Conway</a></th><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3v13M12 3l7 11h-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Boat</span>Yes, in the side or back yard, or under a carport.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2 6h11v10H2zM13 9h4.5L21 12.5V16h-8"/><circle cx="6" cy="17.5" r="1.8"/><circle cx="17" cy="17.5" r="1.8"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Work truck</span>Yes, but a big work truck may not park on a city street.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Short-term rental</span>Only in some zones: downtown and the business areas, not on home streets.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11l9-6 9 6M5 10v10h14V10M10 20v-5h4v5"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Shed or fence</span>Yes, with a permit, in the back yard. Fences are 4 feet in front and up to 8 in back.</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Loris</th><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3v13M12 3l7 11h-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Boat</span>A boat over 17 feet stays out of the front and side setbacks and 5 feet from the back line.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2 6h11v10H2zM13 9h4.5L21 12.5V16h-8"/><circle cx="6" cy="17.5" r="1.8"/><circle cx="17" cy="17.5" r="1.8"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Work truck</span>Yes, one, up to 2 tons.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Short-term rental</span>Not a listed use in city zoning, and a use not listed is not permitted. We ask the city about the address.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11l9-6 9 6M5 10v10h14V10M10 20v-5h4v5"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Shed or fence</span>Up to two buildings, a garage or carport included, in the side or back yard.</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Aynor</th><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3v13M12 3l7 11h-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Boat</span>The town's zoning does not limit it.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M2 6h11v10H2zM13 9h4.5L21 12.5V16h-8"/><circle cx="6" cy="17.5" r="1.8"/><circle cx="17" cy="17.5" r="1.8"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Work truck</span>No limit in the town's zoning.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Short-term rental</span>Only with approval: the town's zoning does not list short stays, and the zoning appeals board may approve a use of the same general character as a listed one.</span></td><td><span class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11l9-6 9 6M5 10v10h14V10M10 20v-5h4v5"/></svg></span><span><span class="c3-nh-k" aria-hidden="true">Shed or fence</span>Yes, in the back yard, 5 feet from the line.</span></td></tr></tbody></table><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Before you make an offer, we check the town or county rules for that lot, the deed for restrictions and the county records for an HOA.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In <a href="https://library.municode.com/sc/myrtle_beach/codes/code_of_ordinances?nodeId=COOR_APXAZO_ART14ZODI_S1407TAUS" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Myrtle Beach</a>, <a href="https://www.nmb.us/DocumentCenter/View/6133/Rental-Property-Quick-Reference" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">North Myrtle Beach</a> and <a href="https://library.municode.com/sc/surfside_beach/codes/code_of_ordinances?nodeId=VOII_CH17ZO_ARTIIIDIUSRE_DIV11USRE_S17-396.10TRRELOTERE" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Surfside Beach</a>, renting out a home needs a business license. In the towns, you can leave a boat in the driveway for a day to load and unload. On county roads, the county <a href="https://library.municode.com/sc/horry_county/codes/code_of_ordinances?nodeId=COOR_CH13OFMIPR_ARTIINGE_S13-12PRPA" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">bans parking</a> only where it posts a sign.</p><div class="c3-story" style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:1.5rem 1.5rem .7rem;margin:1.4rem 0 1.4rem;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem"><strong>Example:</strong> Teresa wants a home with no HOA and room for her 20-foot boat. She likes a house on a small lot with a Myrtle Beach address.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">Her Chapter3 agent finds the house on the county map, inside the city of Myrtle Beach. The city's front-yard rule applies to her boat, and that lot has no other room for it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">The agent shows her houses outside the city limits, under the county's rules. Teresa makes an offer on one with a wide side yard.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Prices">What does a house with no HOA fee cost?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The largest group, about 280 houses, is listed from $250,000 to $500,000, most of them around Conway, Loris and Aynor. The rest:</p><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">About 60 houses for sale under $250,000, most of them built before 1990 and about half in and around Conway.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">About 130 from $500,000 to $750,000, a third of them within half a mile of the beach.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">About 220 at $750,000 and up, about 2 in 3 of them within half a mile of the beach.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our guide to the <a href="/buyers/affordable-places-to-live/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">most affordable places to buy near Myrtle Beach</a> compares the towns.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the homes with no HOA fee in your price range.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us your range and the areas you like. One of our agents sends the homes for sale in it.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Get the list</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="what-do-you-give-up-with-no-hoa"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What you give up">What do you give up with no HOA?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No HOA means no shared pool, clubhouse or gate, and no HOA rules for your neighbors' houses either. A home with no HOA can still have deed restrictions on what you build or keep there.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you want a pool, a clubhouse or a gate, you pay an HOA fee for them. A pool of your own needs no HOA: our <a href="/buyers/pool-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">guide to homes with a pool</a> shows where they are. Many houses near the sand have no HOA fee either, as our <a href="/buyers/homes-near-the-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">guide to houses near the beach</a> shows. Our guides to the <a href="/buyers/best-neighborhoods/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">best neighborhoods for what you want nearby</a> and to <a href="/buyers/gated-communities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">gated communities around Myrtle Beach</a> show where to look. Our guide to <a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/the-farm/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The Farm at Carolina Forest</a> shows one Carolina Forest neighborhood, and our guide to <a href="/hoa/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">what HOA fees cover</a> explains each part of a fee.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="homes-with-no-hoa-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Homes with no HOA FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I park a boat at my house in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, on your own lot, within the rule of the town it is in; the table under What can you do at home gives each one.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which areas near Myrtle Beach almost always have an HOA?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Carolina Forest, the Grande Dunes, the Market Common and Burgess: almost every home for sale there has an HOA fee. Almost all homes for sale in Little River's named subdivisions have an HOA fee too. Longs and the country around Conway look rural, but most homes for sale there have an HOA fee too.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Are there homes with no HOA in Murrells Inlet?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, but only a little more than 1 in 4 homes for sale with a Murrells Inlet address is listed with no HOA fee. At the north end of the inlet, by the creeks and the Stanley Drive landing, almost every house for sale has none.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Are there homes with no HOA in North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. More than half of the homes for sale with a North Myrtle Beach address are listed with no HOA fee. Almost all of them are in Cherry Grove, Crescent Beach, Windy Hill and Ocean Drive.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is a typical HOA fee in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About $95 a month on a house. A condo fee is much higher because it includes the building's insurance, water and sewer, trash and a pool.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you buy a condo with no HOA fee in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Almost never. Of about 2,700 condos for sale around Myrtle Beach, only one was listed with no HOA fee. South Carolina law makes condo owners share the cost of the building.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Does a listing with no HOA fee mean the home has no HOA?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not always. A blank fee means no fee was listed. We check the deed and the county records for an HOA before you make an offer.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is a campground home with no HOA fee a no-HOA home?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. A campground home has no HOA fee, but it sits on leased land, and you pay a yearly lease for the land under it.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://library.municode.com/sc/horry_county/codes/code_of_ordinances" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">town and county codes</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/parksandrecreation/boat-landings/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county boat landings</a>, <a href="https://library.municode.com/sc/horry_county/codes/code_of_ordinances?nodeId=COOR_APXBZO_ARTIXCOUS_S927HOOC" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county home business rule</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t27c031.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">S.C. condominium law</a>, <a href="https://www.solidwasteauthority.org/residential.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">trash service</a>, <a href="https://www.scencyclopedia.org/sce/entries/north-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">S.C. Encyclopedia</a>. Homes for sale in the local MLS, on October 13, 2026; list prices; homes on leased land left out. Areas are MLS areas or a distance from a town center or a boat landing; flood zones and lots from county and federal maps. Drive times without traffic. Not legal advice.</p><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">A two-story white wood house with long porches on both floors, shaded by big oak trees with Spanish moss, on Broadway Street in downtown Myrtle Beach. Photo: Pubdog, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pleasant_Inn_Myrtle_Beach_SC_Jun_10.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>. Chapter3 Realty blurred the house number and resized the photo.</div><div role="listitem">An older two-story house with columns on North Ocean Boulevard, in the Myrtle Heights-Oak Park Historic District. Photo: Pubdog, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Myrtle_Heights-Oak_Park_Historic_District_3701_N._Ocean_Blvd._Jun_10.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>. Chapter3 Realty blurred the house number and resized the photo.</div><div role="listitem">Streets of two-story beach houses among trees behind the oceanfront at Crescent Beach in North Myrtle Beach, seen from a plane over the ocean. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Geological Survey</a>.</div><div role="listitem">Rows of houses on long canals with boat docks, running back from the beach to a wide green marsh at Cherry Grove, seen from a plane over the ocean. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Geological Survey</a>.</div><div role="listitem">The old Little River waterfront from the air: streets of houses beside the salt marsh and the Intracoastal Waterway. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty exported this view, added two labels and adjusted the contrast.</div><div role="listitem">Beach houses in rows between the ocean beach and a wide marsh with tidal creeks and boat docks at Garden City Beach, seen from a plane over the ocean. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Geological Survey</a>.</div><div role="listitem">The Riverwalk in downtown Conway, on the Waccamaw River. Photo: Pubdog, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Waccamaw_River_Warehouse_Historic_District_Jun_10.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>.</div><div role=