ol is east of US 17, the highway along the coast. Of all houses for sale, about 1 in 6 is.</p><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-n/buyers-pool-homes/surfside-beach-houses-with-pools-2011-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-n/buyers-pool-homes/surfside-beach-houses-with-pools-2011-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-n/buyers-pool-homes/surfside-beach-houses-with-pools-2011-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="675" alt="Four beach houses in a row, each with a small fenced pool between the house and the dunes, with wooden walkways over the dunes to the beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="USGS photo, 2011. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">USGS photo, 2011</a></span></div><figcaption>Four oceanfront houses in Surfside Beach, each with its own pool behind the dunes, seen from a plane in 2011.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Surfside Beach and the Garden City area have the highest share. In each, 1 house in 4 or more for sale has its own pool.</p></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We checked every house for sale on our site on November 8, 2026 and counted the ones that list their own pool:</p><table class="pl-towns"><caption>Houses for sale with their own pool, by town</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Town</th><th scope="col">With a pool</th><th scope="col">Middle asking price, with a pool</th><th scope="col">Middle asking price, no pool</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;city=Myrtle%20Beach&amp;has=pool,county_horry">Myrtle Beach</a></th><td data-l="With a pool">113 of 1,049</td><td data-l="Middle price, with a pool">$1,120,000</td><td data-l="Middle price, no pool">$460,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;city=North%20Myrtle%20Beach&amp;has=pool,county_horry">North Myrtle Beach</a></th><td data-l="With a pool">47 of 257</td><td data-l="Middle price, with a pool">$1,000,000</td><td data-l="Middle price, no pool">$650,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;has=pool,area_carolina_forest,county_horry">Carolina Forest area</a></th><td data-l="With a pool">33 of 300</td><td data-l="Middle price, with a pool">$985,000</td><td data-l="Middle price, no pool">$465,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;city=Conway&amp;has=pool,county_horry">Conway</a></th><td data-l="With a pool">23 of 643</td><td data-l="Middle price, with a pool">$515,000</td><td data-l="Middle price, no pool">$325,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;city=Surfside%20Beach&amp;has=pool,county_horry">Surfside Beach</a></th><td data-l="With a pool">21 of 84</td><td data-l="Middle price, with a pool">$1,250,000</td><td data-l="Middle price, no pool">$500,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;city=Murrells%20Inlet&amp;has=pool,county_horry">Murrells Inlet, Horry County side</a></th><td data-l="With a pool">20 of 134</td><td data-l="Middle price, with a pool">$1,000,000</td><td data-l="Middle price, no pool">$530,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;city=Longs&amp;has=pool,county_horry">Longs</a></th><td data-l="With a pool">14 of 325</td><td data-l="Middle price, with a pool">$435,000</td><td data-l="Middle price, no pool">$320,000</td></tr><tr><th scope="row"><a href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;has=pool,area_garden_city,county_horry">Garden City area</a></th><td data-l="With a pool">11 of 36</td><td data-l="Middle price, with a pool">$1,000,000</td><td data-l="Middle price, no pool">$730,000</td></tr><tr class="all"><th scope="row">All of Horry County</th><td data-l="With a pool">257 of 2,950</td><td data-l="Middle price, with a pool">$955,000</td><td data-l="Middle price, no pool">$400,000</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="pl-note">A town here is the mailing address, not the city limits. Carolina Forest and Garden City are areas, not towns, and they overlap the towns. Above-ground pools are not counted. Each name opens its pool homes on our map.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Little River (8), Loris (5), Socastee area (4) and Aynor (1) each had fewer than 10, too few for a middle price. Across the county line in Georgetown County, 16 of the 117 houses for sale in <a href="/homes/map/?q=house%20with%20a%20pool%20in%20pawleys%20island" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Pawleys Island</a> have a pool.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Prices">How much does a house with a pool cost in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A private pool comes mostly with the top of the market. Over $1,000,000, more than half of houses for sale have one.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Share of houses for sale with their own pool, by asking price"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Share of houses for sale with their own pool, by asking price</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Asking price</span><span role="columnheader">share with a pool</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">$300,000 or less</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.013" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">1%</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">$300,000 to $400,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.029" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">2%</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">$400,000 to $500,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.043" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">3%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">$500,000 to $750,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.107" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">8%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">$750,000 to $1,000,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.371" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">26%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">$1,000,000 to $1,500,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.663" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">46%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">$1,500,000 to $2,000,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.851" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">60%</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Over $2,000,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.997" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">70%</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Houses for sale in Horry County, our count. Under $500,000 the bars are gray.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At the same size, a house with a pool still asks far more. Houses of 1,500 to 1,999 square feet ask about $515,000 with a pool and $350,000 without. At 3,000 to 3,999 square feet it is about $1,120,000 against $775,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">That gap is not the price of a pool. Houses with a pool are more often on the water, about 1 in 5 against 1 in 7.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Is that pool house priced right?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send us the listing. We set its asking price beside the houses most like it nearby, with and without a pool.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us price a pool house</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="own-or-shared"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Own or shared">Should you buy a house with a pool or use a community pool?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house with its own pool asks more than twice as much in the middle as one in a neighborhood with a shared pool.</p><ul class="pl-cards" aria-label="Your own pool or a neighborhood pool"><li><span class="k">Your own pool</span><b>Swim when you like, and keep it up yourself</b><p>You pay for the chemicals, the repairs, the fence and the power for the pump. A pool pump can use as much as $310 of electricity a year.</p><p>About 1 in 4 of these houses also lists a hot tub.</p></li><li><span class="k">A neighborhood pool</span><b>Swim down the street, and the HOA keeps it up</b><p>The middle homeowners association (HOA) fee in these neighborhoods is about $105 a month. The middle asking price of their houses is about $435,000.</p><p>The state requires a yearly permit for the pool, and a certified pool operator checks it at least three times a week while it is open.</p></li></ul><div class="pl-stat"><p class="k">On a budget of $500,000 or less</p><ul><li><strong>37</strong><span>houses for sale with their own pool, in all of Horry County</span></li><li><strong>827</strong><span>houses for sale in a neighborhood with a shared pool</span></li></ul></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="neighborhoods"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Neighborhoods">Which neighborhoods near Myrtle Beach have a shared pool?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Five of them follow, from the lowest middle price to the highest. Each name opens its houses for sale on our map. The counts are from the same day as the town table.</p><ul class="pl-plain pl-nb" aria-label="Five neighborhoods with a shared pool"><li><b><a href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;subdivision=Golf%20%26%20Yacht&amp;has=county_horry">Myrtle Beach Golf and Yacht Club</a>, off Bay Road near Socastee</b>Mostly one-story houses behind a gatehouse. Owners share a pool and a hot tub, open April 15 to October 15, with tennis courts and a community center. Of its 11 houses for sale, 9 asked $300,000 or less. <a class="pl-ask" href="/contact/">Have us send you its houses for sale as they list</a></li><li><b><a href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;subdivision=Carolina%20Forest%20-%20The%20Farm&amp;has=county_horry">The Farm at Carolina Forest</a></b>The HOA has a large pool and a small pool. Its rules allow no private pool on a lot, so owners swim at these. Its 15 houses for sale had a middle asking price of about $350,000. Our <a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/the-farm/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">guide to The Farm</a> has its fee and rules. <a class="pl-ask" href="/contact/">Have us find you a house in The Farm</a></li><li><b><a href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;subdivision=Berkshire%20Forest&amp;has=county_horry">Berkshire Forest</a>, in Carolina Forest</b>Two pool areas. The first, beside a lake, has a pool with a water slide. The second has a pool and pickleball courts. 13 of its 17 houses for sale asked $500,000 or less. <a class="pl-ask" href="/contact/">Have us show you houses in Berkshire Forest</a></li><li><b><a href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;subdivision=Waterbridge&amp;has=county_horry">Waterbridge</a>, in Carolina Forest</b>Its HOA describes a swimming pool complex, pocket parks and over 80 acres of lakes and natural areas. Its 27 houses for sale had a middle asking price of about $680,000. <a class="pl-ask" href="/contact/">Have us price a house in Waterbridge</a></li><li><b><a href="/homes/map/?type=house&amp;subdivision=Plantation%20Lakes&amp;has=county_horry">Plantation Lakes</a>, in Carolina Forest</b>Two large pools joined by waterfalls, a clubhouse with a gym, and lakes where owners take out pontoon boats. 5 of its 14 houses for sale also have a pool of their own. <a class="pl-ask" href="/contact/">Have us set up a search in Plantation Lakes</a></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each community on our <a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">55+ communities page</a> also has its own clubhouse and pool.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="upkeep"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Upkeep">What does a pool cost to keep up in Horry County?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A pool adds power, care and insurance to your bills. A pool you add later also raises your property tax.</p><ul class="pl-plain" aria-label="What a pool adds to the cost of owning"><li><b>Power for the pump</b>The pump can be a home's second largest user of energy. An <a href="https://www.energystar.gov/products/pool_pumps" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ENERGY STAR</a> certified in-ground pump uses about 20 percent less and saves about $50 a year.</li><li><b>Chemicals and care</b>Each pool service company charges its own price for weekly care and chemicals. We get a quote for the house you want before you make an offer.</li><li><b>Insurance</b>Tell your insurer about the pool before you buy. A pool can raise the premium, and the insurer can ask whether it is covered or locked when no one is using it, and what fence you have. An umbrella policy adds liability coverage above your homeowners policy.</li><li><b>Property tax</b>A pool that is already there is part of the home's value for tax. If you add a pool after you buy, the county adds its full value to your home's value. There is a 15 percent limit on how much the county can raise a home's value at a countywide revaluation. It does not cover the new pool in its first taxed year. Our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax page</a> has the rates.</li></ul><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">What will this pool cost you to keep?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us which house. We get a quote from a pool service company and ask the seller for the pool's repair bills.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us get a pool service quote</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="fence"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Fence rule">Do you need a fence around a pool in Horry County?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Outside city limits, Horry County requires a fence or other barrier with gates around a pool. The county uses the 2021 International Swimming Pool and Spa Code.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside a city such as Myrtle Beach or North Myrtle Beach, the city's own building official issues the pool permit. South Carolina has no statewide pool code, so each city decides its own rule. We ask the city's building office about the house you want.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We read the county's pool fence form, which quotes the code, and drew its rule:</p><figure class="pl-fig"><p class="cap">Horry County's pool fence rule, outside city limits</p><div class="pl-fig-in"><svg class="pl-svg" viewBox="0 0 480 360" role="img" aria-labelledby="plSvgT" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><title id="plSvgT">Drawing of a backyard pool from above: the house wall on one side and a fence on the other three, a gate that swings out, and the pump outside the fence. The words House, Pool and Outside the fence label the parts. Numbers 1 to 6 match the list.</title><rect x="0" y="0" width="480" height="360" rx="18" fill="#fbf8f3"/><rect x="40" y="82" width="360" height="218" fill="#e3ecd6"/><rect x="20" y="16" width="400" height="66" rx="4" fill="#e8dfd2" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="228" y="70" width="34" height="12" rx="2" fill="#c4783a"/><rect x="112" y="128" width="196" height="116" rx