offset:2px}</style><style>section[style*="background:var(--ivory)"] .c3ph-card{background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-cards{max-width:920px}.c3ph-card strong{font-family:var(--sans)}.c3ph-card span.c3ph-t{font-size:1rem!important}.c3ph-card strong{font-size:1rem!important}ul[role=list] li span[style*="font-size:.9rem"]{font-size:1rem!important}section#c3-photo{padding-top:0}section:has(+section#c3-photo){background:var(--ivory-2)!important;padding-bottom:2rem}.c3ph-hero{margin:0}.c3-aerial .c3ph-hero{max-width:900px;margin:1.4rem 0 1.6rem}.c3-aerial .c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:auto!important;height:auto}.c3-aerial-close .c3ph-hero{max-width:640px}.c3-aerial-ctop .c3ph-cr{top:0;bottom:auto;padding:.35rem .6rem 1.6rem 2.6rem;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 0%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0))}@media (max-width:699px){.c3ph-cards>:last-child:nth-child(odd){grid-column:1/-1}}.c3-maps{display:grid;gap:0 1.5rem;max-width:1136px}@media (min-width:900px){.c3-maps{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-maps figure{max-width:none!important;margin:1.4rem 0 .4rem!important}.c3-maps svg,.c3-maps img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.c3-map-links{row-gap:0!important}.c3-map-links a{padding:.55rem 0}ul[role=list][style*="minmax(13rem,1fr)"]{grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(min(13rem,100%),1fr))!important}</style><style>.c3-aerial .c3ph-hero,.c3-aerial-close .c3ph-hero{max-width:720px}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Spring and early summer are the busiest months for home sales in Horry County. From 2021 to 2025, about 38 percent of home resales were recorded in March through June. That is more than in any other four months in a row. An even spread would be 33 percent.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Home sales recorded each month, 2021 to 2025"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Home sales recorded each month, 2021 to 2025</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Month</span><span role="columnheader">home sales recorded</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">January</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.684" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">4,363</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">February</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.689" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">4,397</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">March</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.991" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">6,324</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">April</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.96" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">6,130</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">May</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.992" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">6,333</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">June</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">6,383</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">July</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.859" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">5,486</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">August</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.915" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">5,838</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">September</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.855" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">5,458</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">October</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.843" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">5,380</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">November</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.749" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">4,778</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">December</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.751" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">4,794</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Horry County, the five years added together, from our count of county deeds. Resales only: builders' sales of new homes are left out. March to June, the four busiest months, are in color.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">January and February are the slowest months. Together they hold about 13 percent of a year's sales.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The pattern is not the same every year. In 2025, sales were spread more evenly, and October was the busiest month. Prices still followed the season that year. February was again the lowest month for price, and houses that closed in June and July still sold above the months around them.</p><h3 id="price-by-month" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Which month brings the highest price?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">June brought the highest middle price, and February the lowest. Half of the homes sold for more than the middle price, and half for less.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">February was lower than the months around it in all five years. May and June were higher in four of the five.</p><figure class="bt-fig bt-div"><p class="cap" id="btDivCap">How much more or less homes sold for in each month</p><div role="table" aria-labelledby="btDivCap"><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Month</span><span role="columnheader">Middle price, higher or lower than nearby months</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row" class="neg"><span role="rowheader">Jan</span><span role="cell"><span class="tr" aria-hidden="true"><span class="b" style="width:10.6%"></span></span><span class="v">1.1% lower</span></span></div><div role="row" class="neg"><span role="rowheader">Feb</span><span role="cell"><span class="tr" aria-hidden="true"><span class="b" style="width:43.3%"></span></span><span class="v">4.3% lower</span></span></div><div role="row" class="neg"><span role="rowheader">Mar</span><span role="cell"><span class="tr" aria-hidden="true"><span class="b" style="width:14.5%"></span></span><span class="v">1.5% lower</span></span></div><div role="row" class="pos"><span role="rowheader">Apr</span><span role="cell"><span class="tr" aria-hidden="true"><span class="b" style="width:3.6%"></span></span><span class="v">0.4% higher</span></span></div><div role="row" class="pos"><span role="rowheader">May</span><span role="cell"><span class="tr" aria-hidden="true"><span class="b" style="width:19.6%"></span></span><span class="v">2.0% higher</span></span></div><div role="row" class="pos"><span role="rowheader">Jun</span><span role="cell"><span class="tr" aria-hidden="true"><span class="b" style="width:22.1%"></span></span><span class="v">2.2% higher</span></span></div><div role="row" class="pos"><span role="rowheader">Jul</span><span role="cell"><span class="tr" aria-hidden="true"><span class="b" style="width:15.5%"></span></span><span class="v">1.6% higher</span></span></div><div role="row" class="pos"><span role="rowheader">Aug</span><span role="cell"><span class="tr" aria-hidden="true"><span class="b" style="width:12.9%"></span></span><span class="v">1.3% higher</span></span></div><div role="row" class="pos"><span role="rowheader">Sep</span><span role="cell"><span class="tr" aria-hidden="true"><span class="b" style="width:16.6%"></span></span><span class="v">1.7% higher</span></span></div><div role="row" class="neg"><span role="rowheader">Oct</span><span role="cell"><span class="tr" aria-hidden="true"><span class="b" style="width:1.7%"></span></span><span class="v">0.2% lower</span></span></div><div role="row" class="neg"><span role="rowheader">Nov</span><span role="cell"><span class="tr" aria-hidden="true"><span class="b" style="width:2.9%"></span></span><span class="v">0.3% lower</span></span></div><div role="row" class="neg"><span role="rowheader">Dec</span><span role="cell"><span class="tr" aria-hidden="true"><span class="b" style="width:9.5%"></span></span><span class="v">1.0% lower</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>We took out the yearly rise in prices, so only the month shows. Averages for 2021 to 2025, from county deeds.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From February's bar to June's bar is about 6 percent. On a home at the county's middle resale price of about $305,000, that is about $20,000. Part of that gap comes from which homes sell in each month, so one home should expect less. We could not measure how much less.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="when-to-list"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="When to list">When should you list to close in the best months?</h2><div class="bt-side"><div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">List about three months before the month you want to close. A home is under contract, which agents call pending, once the buyer and the seller have both signed the purchase contract.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Homes go under contract fastest in March, April and May. This spring, the middle home had a buyer after about 6 to 7 weeks on the market. In the years before, it was about 4 weeks.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">After a buyer signs, closing took about five weeks here, in every month of the year. A buyer who pays cash has no lender to wait for. Our page on <a href="/sell/cash-offer/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">cash offers</a> covers that kind of sale.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The table counts back from a closing in the middle of each month, at the pace of the last 12 months. Winter closings need up to 4 months. The four busiest months are in bold.</p></div><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">To close in the middle of</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Put the home on the market in</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">January</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">late September</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">February</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">late October</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><b>March</b></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><b>early December</b></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><b>April</b></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><b>late January</b></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><b>May</b></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><b>late February</b></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><b>June</b></td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><b>mid March</b></td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">July</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">mid April</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">August</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">mid May</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">September</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">mid June</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">October</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">mid July</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">November</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">mid August</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">December</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">mid September</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A worked example: to close in early June, count back about 5 weeks to a signed contract in late April. Count back about 6 to 7 weeks more, and the house goes on the market in mid March.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Start getting the home ready a few weeks before that. Our page on <a href="/sell/repairs-before-selling/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">repairs before selling</a> lists what to fix first.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory-2);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Have us set a listing date for a May or June closing</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us when you need to be out, and we will work back to the day your home should go on the market.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us work back from my date</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="condo-or-house"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Condo or house">Is the best month different for a condo?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Condos here sell for the most in April and May, a little earlier in the year than houses, which sell for the most in June.</p><ul class="bt-cards" aria-label="When a condo and a house sell for the most"><li><span class="k">A condo</span><b>Close in April or May. List in late January or February.</b><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Condos that closed in April and May sold for the highest middle prices of the year, about 9 percent above February's.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If you rent the condo by the night, a spring sale gives up the summer. In all eight towns in our rental data, nightly rentals earn the most in July.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Renting through the summer and selling in the fall has a cost too. Condos that closed from September to November sold for about the same as the months around them, not the spring high.</p></li><li><span class="k">A house or townhome</span><b>Close in June. List in March.</b><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Houses that closed in June sold for the highest middle price of the year, about 5 percent above February's.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">July and September closings did nearly as well. All three months were above the months around them in all five years.</p></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our page on <a href="/sell/sell-my-condo/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">selling a condo</a> covers the rest of a condo sale: the HOA papers, rental programs and buyers' loans.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="winter"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Winter">Is winter a bad time to sell a house in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Winter has fewer sales and lower prices. It also has fewer homes for sale to compete with yours.</p><ul class="bt-plain" aria-label="What winter means for a seller"><li><b>Fewer sales, lower prices</b>January and February have the fewest sales of the year. February closings sold for the lowest middle price of the year.</li><li><b>Fewer homes for sale</b>In the Myrtle Beach area, December has the fewest new listings of the year, less than half of April's. Buyers still sign contracts all winter, about 640 in a typical December.</li><li><b>Out-of-state buyers buy all year</b>About 3 in 10 buyers in every month are from another state. Our page on <a href="/sell/out-of-state-buyers/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">out-of-state buyers</a> says where they come from.</li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A home that goes under contract in February closes about five weeks later, in March or early April, when the busy months begin.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="hurricane-season"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Hurricane season">Does hurricane season hurt a home sale here?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not as a season. Atlantic <a href="https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/climo/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">hurricane season</a> is June 1 to November 30. Most of the season's activity comes between mid-August and mid-October, with the peak on September 10.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Those months are not a slow season for home sales. August, September and October each had about 8 to 9 percent of a year's home resales. August and September closings sold a little above the months around them on average.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What happened to home sales the week Hurricane Ian came?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Hurricane Ian came ashore near Georgetown on Friday, September 30, 2022. The county recorded no home sales that day. It recorded sales again the next Monday, and the week after the storm had more sales than the week before.</p><figure class="bt-fig bt-ian"><p class="cap">Home sales recorded each working day around Hurricane Ian, 2022</p><div class="wks" role="img" aria-label="Home sales recorded each working day from September 19 to October 14, 2022. 97 on Thursday, September 29, none on Friday, September 30, the day Ian came ashore, then 64 and 94 the next Monday and Tuesday. Week totals: 258, 239, 317, 228."><div class="wk"><div class="bars"><span class="bar" style="height:49%"></span><span class="bar" style="height:53%"></span><span class="bar" style="height:47%"></span><span class="bar" style="height:56%"></span><span class="bar" style="height:61%"></span></div><p class="t"><span>Sep 19 to Sep 23</span><b>258</b></p></div><div class="wk"><div class="bars"><span class="bar" style="height:25%"></span><span class="bar" style="height:80%"></span><span class="bar" style="height:41%"></span><span class="bar" style="height:100%"></span><span class="bar zero"><b class="lb">Ian</b></span></div><p class="t"><span>Sep 26 to Sep 30</span><b>239</b></p></div><div class="wk"><div class="bars"><span class="bar" style="height:66%"></span><span class="bar" style="height:97%"></span><span class="bar" style="height:48%"></span><span class="bar" style="height:51%"></span><span class="bar" style="height:65%"></span></div><p class="t"><span>Oct 3 to Oct 7</span><b>317</b></p></div><div class="wk"><div class="bars"><span class="bar" style="height:30%"></span><span class="bar" style="height:40%"></span><span class="bar" style="height:47%"></span><span class="bar" style="height:60%"></span><span class="bar" style="height:58%"></span></div><p class="t"><span>Oct 10 to Oct 14</span><b>228</b></p></div></div><figcaption>Resales recorded by Horry County, Monday to Friday. The dashed line is Friday, September 30, when Ian came ashore and the county recorded none. The number under each week is that week's total.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The storm Debby came ashore down the coast, near Bulls Bay, early on Thursday, August 8, 2024. The county recorded no sales that day and recorded sales again the next day.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A storm can move a closing by a few days, not by a season. What a storm means for a buyer's insurance is on our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance page</a>.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Have us build a few spare days into a fall closing</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">A storm week can push a closing back a few days. Tell us the month you hope to close, and we will plan the dates with room to spare.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us plan my closing dates</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="tourists-and-school"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Tourists and school">Do tourist season and the school year change the best month?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Tourist season peaks in July, after the busiest months for home sales. School lets out in early June, during one of them.</p><div class="bt-side"><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-n/sell-best-time-to-sell/myrtle-beach-beach-in-june-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-n/sell-best-time-to-sell/myrtle-beach-beach-in-june-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-n/sell-best-time-to-sell/myrtle-beach-beach-in-june-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="675" alt="A crowded beach in Myrtle Beach in June, with rental umbrellas, rows of blue beach chairs and oceanfront towers" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Loadmaster. License: CC BY-SA 3.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 3.0">Photo: Loadmaster</a></span></div><figcaption>Myrtle Beach on a June day. Tourist season peaks in July, the month after houses here sell highest.</figcaption></figure></div><ul class="bt-plain" aria-label="Tourist season and the school year"><li><b>Tourist season</b>This year, Horry County had about 40 percent more hotel, restaurant and other leisure jobs in July than in January. Home sales do not follow the tourists: July has fewer sales than June.</li><li><b>The school year</b>Horry County public schools let out in early June and start again in mid-August. This school year ends on June 8, 2027, and the next one starts on August 18, 2027. Make-up days can move the last day.</li><li><b>Moving while school is out</b>June is one of the two busiest months for home sales. To close in June, list in March.</li></ul></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-matters-more"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What matters more">What matters more than the month you sell?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Prices changed far more from year to year than from month to month. The middle price rose about 20 percent from 2021 to 2022, against about 6 percent between February and June.</p><ul class="bt-plain" aria-label="What matters more than the month"><li><b>The year</b>Since 2024 the middle resale price has stayed near $305,000. So far this year it has been about the same again, with about as many sales as a year earlier. Our <a href="/sell/home-value/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">home value page</a> gives middle prices by area.</li><li><b>The market now</b>In September 2026, about 8,000 homes were for sale in the Myrtle Beach area, about the same as a year earlier. Homes went under contract about a week faster than a year earlier.</li><li><b>The asking price</b>That month, about 3 in 10 listings had cut their asking price. Each week a home waits for a cut moves its closing a week later, and can push a spring closing into summer. Buyers paid about 97 to 98 percent of the last asking price, whatever the month. The row of just-listed homes on this page shows what yours would compete with.</li><li><b>Tax dates</b>Owning and living in your main home for 2 of the last 5 years can mean no federal tax on up to $250,000 of your profit. If you are a few months short, selling early can cost that. A rental or second home has its own one-year date. Our <a href="/sell/capital-gains/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">capital gains page</a> explains both, from <a href="https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc701" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS Topic 701</a> and <a href="https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc409" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS Topic 409</a>. Ask a tax pro about your own dates.</li><li><b>Your own dates</b>You may have a date you must move by: a lease that ends, a new job, or a home you are buying. Work back from that date with the weeks above. Our pages on <a href="/sell/sell-or-buy-first/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">whether to sell or buy first</a> and <a href="/sell/rental-property/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">selling a rented home</a> cover those cases.</li></ul><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Have us price it for the month you list</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">We price your home from recorded sales near you and the homes you would compete with that month.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Have us price my home for my month</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="best-time-to-sell-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Best time to sell FAQ</h2><style>.c3-faq details{border-top:1px solid var(--rule,rgba(15,27,45,.14))}.c3-faq details:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule,rgba(15,27,45,.14))}.c3-faq summary{list-style:none;cursor:pointer;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;padding:.2rem 0}.c3-faq summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}.c3-faq summary h3{margin:.9rem 0!important;flex:1}.c3-faq summary::after{content:"+";font:400 1.5rem/1 var(--sans);color:var(--brass);flex:none;width:1.5rem;text-align:center}.c3-faq details[open] summary::after{content:"\2212"}.c3-faq details p{margin:0 0 1rem!important}.c3-faq summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--brass);outline-offset:3px}</style><div class="c3-faq"><details open><summary><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the worst month to sell a house in Myrtle Beach?</h3></summary><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">February. For houses and for condos alike, it was the lowest month of the year for price, and one of the slowest for sales.</p></details><details><summary><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do houses sell in December in Myrtle Beach?</h3></summary><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Buyers sign contracts all winter. A contract signed in December closes about five weeks later, in January.</p></details><details><summary><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How long does it take from contract to closing in Myrtle Beach?</h3></summary><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About five weeks. The average ran from 36 days to 42 days, depending on the month.</p></details><details><summary><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is now a good time to sell a house in Myrtle Beach?</h3></summary><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At this year's pace, a home listed in mid November closes around mid February, the lowest month for price. Listing in March moves the closing to May or June, at the cost of four more months of owning the home.</p></details><details><summary><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">When is the best time to sell a beach condo in Myrtle Beach?</h3></summary><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Close in April or May, when condos sold for the most. That means listing in late January or February, before the summer rental season.</p></details></div><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/search/SearchTypeDocType" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">County deeds</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer/24" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">County parcels</a>, <a href="https://www.zillow.com/research/data/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zillow Research</a>, <a href="https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/climo/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA hurricane climatology</a>, <a href="https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/data/tcr/AL092022_Ian.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NHC Ian report</a>, <a href="https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/data/tcr/AL042024_Debby.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NHC Debby report</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountyschools.net/about-hcs/hcs-calendars" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County Schools calendars</a>, <a href="https://download.bls.gov/pub/time.series/sm/sm.data.42.SouthCarolina" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BLS jobs</a>, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc701" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS Topic 701</a>, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/taxtopics/tc409" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS Topic 409</a>. Sales by month and middle prices: our count of county deeds, 2021 to 2025. Rental months: AirROI, in our rental data.</p><div class="bt-notes"><p class="bt-small"><strong>How we counted.</strong> We read the county's index of every deed recorded since 2019 and counted 65,664 home resales from 2021 to 2025. A resale is a deed of $10,000 or more for one home that the county lists today as residential, with a building on it.</p><p class="bt-small">We left out 21,968 sales by builders, whose closings are spread more evenly over the year. We also left out tax sales, foreclosures, corrective deeds and sales under 30 percent of the county's value.</p><p class="bt-small">Of the 65,664 resales, about 37,400 were houses and townhomes and 28,300 condos. We told a condo from a house by the county's parcel records.</p><p class="bt-small">Each sale is counted in the month the county recorded its deed, which comes after the closing. The county's index carries a parcel number on nearly every deed only from July 2020, so our count starts in 2021. The price chart compares each month's middle price with the six months before it and the six after. That takes out the rise from year to year.</p><p class="bt-small">Days to a contract and to closing, new listings and price cuts are Zillow's figures for the Myrtle Beach area. The listing table uses Zillow's figures for the latest 12 months.</p><p class="bt-small"><strong>Legal notice.</strong> Chapter3 Realty Corp is a licensed South Carolina real estate brokerage. We are not tax advisers, and nothing on this page is tax or legal advice.</p></div><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Myrtle Beach on a June day. Photo: Loadmaster (David R. Tribble), <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CC BY-SA 3.0</a>, via <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlantic_Ocean_shoreline_in_Myrtle_Beach,_South_Carolina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wikimedia Commons</a>. Chapter3 Realty cropped and resized the photo.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-n/sell-best-time-to-sell/myrtle-beach-beach-in-june-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-n/sell-best-time-to-sell/myrtle-beach-beach-in-june-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":675,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"Myrtle Beach on a June day","caption":"Myrtle Beach on a June day. Tourist season peaks in July, the month after houses here sell highest.","description":"A crowded beach in Myrtle Beach in June, with rental umbrellas, rows of blue beach chairs and oceanfront towers","creator":{"@type":"Person","name":"Loadmaster (David R. Tribble)"},"creditText":"Loadmaster (David R","copyrightNotice":"© Loadmaster (David R. Tribble), CC BY-SA 3.0","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","acquireLicensePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlantic_Ocean_shoreline_in_Myrtle_Beach,_South_Carolina.jpg","isBasedOn":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Atlantic_Ocean_shoreline_in_Myrtle_Beach,_South_Carolina.jpg","contentLocation":{"@type":"Place","name":"Oceanfront, south Myrtle Beach, Myrtle Beach, South Carolina"},"representativeOfPage":true}]}</script></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Have us plan your sale from listing day to closing</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">Tell us when you need to move. We work out the week to list and price your home from recorded sales near it.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="/contact/">Have us plan my sale</a></div></section></main>
